      "writtenOn": "2025-11-06T17:13:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e unsigned char (or just u8)?\n\nmakes sense, will change.\n\n\u003e We must make sure the address, not just the size, is page-aligned?\n\nIf I understand correctly, the percpu implementation guarantees that it will be page aligned as the size is PAGE_SIZE. But I will verify it.\n\n\u003e So maybe there\u0027s nothing wrong in keeping all possible params (including iommu-specific structures) defined in a centralized place in union pkvm_pv_param instead?\n\nThe reason I chose this is because the existing union had kvm specific structures and was fine when this was defined only for kvm. But when I pulled it out for generic usage, I had to bring the kvm specific structures to non-kvm code as well. Its doable but I felt it as a bit unclean.\n\n\u003e Whereas with this new interface, the caller needs to take care not to exceed PAGE_SIZE.\n\nThis is a valid argument. Either I could expose kvm.h to users of this interface or I can put a build time error and explicit comments for the users of this api. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "897d7d49_b81c9a9a",
      "revId": "2386b09dc42f14d09ce2d37b71c6abbfaefec1a3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
