      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The reason I chose this is because the existing union had kvm specific structures and was fine when this was defined only for kvm. But when I pulled it out for generic usage, I had to bring the kvm specific structures to non-kvm code as well. Its doable but I felt it as a bit unclean.\n\nThose IOMMU hypercalls are still pKVM-specific, and pKVM is a part of KVM, so I don\u0027t see much problem with that. By the way:\n\n```\n$ grep -r asm/kvm drivers/iommu/\ndrivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3-kvm.c:#include \u003casm/kvm_pkvm.h\u003e\ndrivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3-kvm.c:#include \u003casm/kvm_mmu.h\u003e\ndrivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/pkvm/arm_smmu_v3.h:#include \u003casm/kvm_asm.h\u003e\ndrivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/pkvm/io-pgtable-arm.c:#include \u003casm/kvm_hyp.h\u003e\ndrivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/pkvm/io-pgtable-arm.c:#include \u003casm/kvm_mmu.h\u003e\ndrivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/pkvm/arm-smmu-v3-module.h:#include \u003casm/kvm_pkvm_module.h\u003e\ndrivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/pkvm/arm-smmu-v3.c:#include \u003casm/kvm_hyp.h\u003e\n```",
      "parentUuid": "3cd0c69f_365775b8",
