      "message": "\u003e Those IOMMU hypercalls are still pKVM-specific, and pKVM is a part of KVM, so I don\u0027t see much problem with that\n\nkvm_pkvm.h seems to be mostly for kvm to pkvm interaction and for handling kvm offloading to pkvm to manage its VMs, while the direct host to pkvm interaction is a different relationship where host as a vm talks to its hypervisor. Thats the reason I thought it was a bit unclean.\n\nI see the precedence you showed for arm, and I am fine doing it that way. Let me see how I can refactor the code to keep the union as it is.",
